# MDD Protocol (Router)

This workspace uses **Markdown-Driven Development (MDD)**. All non-trivial work follows **Plan → Review → Implement → Log**. Keep the always-loaded rule minimal; load detailed methodology on-demand via skills.

## Authority Hierarchy (Truth Precedence)

| Rank | Source | Role |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `docs/_ai_context/knowledge/` | Canonical domain truth |
| 2 | `docs/_ai_context/state/` | Current execution state |
| 3 | Manifests & indexes | Navigation only |
| 4 | `.cursor/rules/` + `.cursor/skills/` | Behavioral guidance |

## Skill Activation (When to Use What)

| When you are… | Use this skill |
|---|---|
| Setting up MDD conventions / governance | `.cursor/skills/mdd-workflow` |
| Creating plans / phase specs | `.cursor/skills/plan-generation` |
| Executing a phase plan / running documented steps | `.cursor/skills/phase-execution` |
| Parsing data files / consuming structured data | `.cursor/skills/data-verification` |
| Starting a session / loading context efficiently | `.cursor/skills/context-loading` |
| Managing canonical knowledge repositories | `.cursor/skills/knowledge-repo` |
| Managing backlog and priorities | `.cursor/skills/backlog-management` |
| Logging work + lessons learned | `.cursor/skills/work-logging` |
| Improving prompts / workflow efficiency | `.cursor/skills/prompt-optimization` |

## Directory Convention

**MDD_ROOT = `docs/_ai_context`**

- `docs/_ai_context/state/`: `MASTER_STATE.md`, `WORK_LOG.md`, `BACKLOG.md`, `repo-manifest.json`
- `docs/_ai_context/analysis/`: plans, debug logs, completion docs (`archive/` for superseded)
- `docs/_ai_context/prompts/`: reusable prompts (including `phases/`)
- `docs/_ai_context/knowledge/`: canonical reference data (human approval for changes)
- `docs/_ai_context/templates/`: standardized artifact templates

To change the root path across skill files, run:

```bash
.cursor/skills/scripts/set-mdd-root.sh "your/custom/path/"
```

## Quick Prohibitions (Keep You Honest)

- Don’t guess file paths; use manifests or search.
- Don’t skip validation; run the gate checks you claim.
- Don’t duplicate existing functionality; reuse before writing new code.
